Faster scan conversion of paths (the edge list rasterizer), for vector heavy pages.

- The active edge list holds copies of the edges instead of pointers into the global edge list,
  and stays nearly sorted (edges that end are removed in place), so it is sorted by an insertion
  sort only when edges crossed; new edges are merged in.
- For the usual one-subscanline steps, spans are added and edges advanced in one pass, adding
  each span as the sum of two points so the loop doesn't branch on where spans start and end.
- The division by the horizontal subsampling is by a constant for the default antialiasing level.
- Scanlines are converted and painted only where the deltas were touched, skipping runs of zero
  coverage, which painting would leave unchanged.
- The global edge list is sorted with a radix sort.

The coverage computed for every pixel is the same, so the rendered output is unchanged.

